# Agent notes for {{.ProjectName}}

This is an Andurel application. Use the `andurel` CLI to discover the project shape and to read the reference patterns instead of inventing file paths, URLs, or generator names.

Frontend: Inertia ({{.Inertia}}) + Vite. HTTP: `net/http` via `pkg/anduin` — handlers are `func(ctx context.Context) error`. There is no Echo and no Fx. Entities validate via `pkg/validation`.

## First-run setup

`andurel new` is offline: it writes files and installs nothing. Complete the documented setup before verifying:

```bash
andurel tool sync          # binaries pinned in andurel.lock
{{.JavaScriptPackageManager}} install              # frontend dependencies
cp .env.example .env       # then set the required values
andurel db create          # only if the database does not exist yet
andurel db migrate up
andurel doctor             # configuration, database, tools, generated code
```

A `.env` file is optional when the same values are exported in the process environment; exported values win. `andurel doctor` reports missing or malformed runtime configuration and an unreachable database as failures, and skips (never passes) a check it could not run.

## Repository policy

- Commit the package manager lockfile ({{if .JavaScriptLockfileName}}`{{.JavaScriptLockfileName}}`{{else}}the lockfile of the selected package manager{{end}}) and use the frozen/immutable install in CI ({{if .JavaScriptFrozenInstallCommand}}`{{.JavaScriptFrozenInstallCommand}}`{{else}}the package manager's frozen mode{{end}}). `andurel new` ships no lockfile; the first install generates it.
- Commit the installed agent skill (for example `./.claude/skills/andurel`). These are project-local references, not caches. Install it with `andurel skill install --harness <harness>` if `andurel new` was run without `--harness`.
- Keep `.env`, `node_modules/`, `bin/`, `dist/` (including `assets/dist`), and `tmp/` out of git.

